=== teeth clauses (each recording is reusable with --replay) ===
--- control
ok:   B1. the replay landed the payload (payloads=1, payload_skips=0) — the contents came back, they were not withheld or refused by name
ok:   B2. the Linux tenant was adopted from the captured context (form=3, stop=spent) — not restarted at _start, and the one-shot stop was spent by the pour
ok:   B3. the resumed copy's FIRST read is at the captured source offset (off=0x30000) — the task continued from the stop, it did not re-enter the copy
ok:   B4. exactly the resumed workload completed: no second [backup] Copying, at least one [backup] Done:
ok:   B5. no [FAULT] in the replay boot
ok:   B6. the tenant's exit tore its address space down (frame(s) freed) — the resumed descriptors and heap were returned, not leaked
ok:   D1. the drill clauses are not applicable: the recording says drill=0 (the plain gate image)
